.TH SDL_PenProximityEvent 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_PenProximityEvent \- Pressure-sensitive pen proximity event structure (event.pproximity.*)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_PenProximityEvent
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_EventType type; /**< SDL_EVENT_PEN_PROXIMITY_IN or SDL_EVENT_PEN_PROXIMITY_OUT */
.BI "    Uint32 reserved;
.BI "    Uint64 timestamp;   /**< In nanoseconds, populated using SDL_GetTicksNS() */
.BI "    SDL_WindowID windowID; /**< The window with pen focus, if any */
.BI "    SDL_PenID which;        /**< The pen instance id */
.BI "    SDL_PenInputFlags pen_state;   /**< Complete pen input state at time of event (added in 3.4.16). */
.BI "    SDL_PenDeviceType device_type; /**< the device type of the pen, if known (added in 3.4.18). */
.BI "} SDL_PenProximityEvent;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
When a pen becomes visible to the system (it is close enough to a tablet, etc), SDL will send an
.BR SDL_EVENT_PEN_PROXIMITY_IN
event with the new pen\(aqs ID\[char46] This ID is valid until the pen leaves proximity again (has been removed from the tablet\(aqs area, the tablet has been unplugged, etc)\[char46] If the same pen reenters proximity again, it will be given a new ID\[char46]
.PP
Note that \(dqproximity\(dq means \(dqclose enough for the tablet to know the tool is there\[char46]\(dq The pen touching and lifting off from the tablet while not leaving the area are handled by
.BR SDL_EVENT_PEN_DOWN
and
.BR SDL_EVENT_PEN_UP \[char46]
.PP
Not all platforms have a window associated with the pen during proximity events\[char46] Some wait until motion/button/etc events to offer this info\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

